WEBVTT

00:02.930 --> 00:05.230
What? You're leaving home for a while?

00:05.460 --> 00:06.350
Yeah.

00:06.720 --> 00:09.730
One of my uncles is sick.

00:09.730 --> 00:11.830
He's pretty old,

00:11.830 --> 00:14.190
so my aunt wants me to visit him.

00:14.190 --> 00:15.910
Can I come with you?

00:15.910 --> 00:16.740
You may not.

00:16.740 --> 00:17.790
Aw.

00:17.790 --> 00:20.650
You always mess things up, Motes.

00:22.210 --> 00:25.840
I'm going to be away from the
house for at least a few days.

00:26.200 --> 00:27.910
So today,

00:29.390 --> 00:33.260
I thought I'd have you learn to do
<i>all</i> of the chores here at Otowakan.

00:39.510 --> 00:41.300
What do you mean?

00:41.300 --> 00:43.070
Everything you see me doing all the time.

00:43.410 --> 00:45.480
Rather, everything <i>you</i>

00:45.480 --> 00:47.770
make me do <i>all by myself</i>, all the time.

00:48.010 --> 00:50.620
Cleaning, laundry, trash,
setting up the bath,

00:50.620 --> 00:53.040
yardwork, replacing the light bulbs...

00:53.040 --> 00:54.810
And I'm always the one doing the notices.

00:54.810 --> 00:57.780
W-W-W-Wait, Kanae.

00:57.780 --> 00:58.380
No!

00:58.380 --> 01:00.200
I'm going to have you learn all of it today!

01:00.610 --> 01:03.980
They say, "Teach a man to fish..."

01:05.220 --> 01:07.610
Well, here at Otowakan, we say,

01:07.610 --> 01:09.300
"Teach a man to do the chores,
or he gets kicked out."

01:09.300 --> 01:10.790
I've never heard of that.

01:10.790 --> 01:13.760
You're learning!

02:48.520 --> 02:51.810
{<b>Otowakan Chores List
Clean the bath - Liszt
Remove cobwebs - Beethes
Weeding - Beethes/Chopin
Mopping - Sousuke/Schubert
Wipe windows - Sousuke
Laundry - Liszt
Wipe chandeliers - Chopin/Schubert
Feed Hasshie-kun - Sousuke
Clean Bathroom - Sousuke</b>

02:49.020 --> 02:50.820
Wh-What the...

02:52.140 --> 02:53.350
There's no love.

02:52.690 --> 02:57.690
11: "At Least Do the Chores"

02:53.350 --> 02:55.490
I sense only malice, my little kitten.

02:55.490 --> 02:56.730
Weeding?

02:56.730 --> 02:57.990
Remove cobwebs?

02:58.320 --> 02:59.500
Me, of all people?

02:59.500 --> 03:02.360
I don't even live here.
Why is my name on the list?

03:02.360 --> 03:06.100
Actually, why isn't my name on
the list when I <i>do</i> live here?

03:07.570 --> 03:10.260
Okay, get back, I'm going to explain.

03:11.020 --> 03:14.030
Like I said, I'm going
to be going away soon.

03:14.340 --> 03:17.730
You will all have to do the chores
yourselves in the meantime.

03:18.070 --> 03:20.070
You better learn them properly.

03:20.340 --> 03:21.470
Any questions?

03:24.490 --> 03:25.630
No one? Good.

03:26.250 --> 03:27.850
Any comments?

03:29.480 --> 03:30.650
No one.

03:30.940 --> 03:33.190
Okay, get started, please.

03:33.190 --> 03:34.470
Wait a second!

03:34.470 --> 03:36.180
I have a comment!

03:37.610 --> 03:38.420
What?

03:38.780 --> 03:42.780
Chores are things people who
<i>live</i> there do, aren't they?

03:42.780 --> 03:45.140
So I don't have...

03:44.380 --> 03:46.320
You don't live here, Sousuke?

03:46.320 --> 03:48.450
Take all your stuff and leave, please.

03:49.710 --> 03:51.080
This sucks.

03:51.080 --> 03:53.670
Why do I get no work,

03:53.670 --> 03:55.830
when Sousuke gets so much?

03:55.830 --> 03:58.460
Your job, Motes, is to not do anything.

03:58.460 --> 03:59.460
What does that mean?

03:59.980 --> 04:03.620
Don't make me engage in such
foolishness as cleaning, girl.

04:04.050 --> 04:05.570
If you really need a hand...

04:05.570 --> 04:07.860
I'll have you leave, if you don't clean.

04:09.130 --> 04:12.810
There are more important things
for me to do, my little kitten.

04:13.230 --> 04:13.950
What?

04:14.260 --> 04:18.280
Listen, this mansion will be without

04:18.280 --> 04:21.200
a symbol while you are gone.

04:21.500 --> 04:24.370
Otowakan without its emblem isn't Otowakan.

04:24.370 --> 04:26.860
Therefore, I intend to focus

04:26.860 --> 04:28.630
on this one task.

04:30.080 --> 04:34.330
Liszt - Symbol

04:30.860 --> 04:32.030
The symbol.

04:32.030 --> 04:34.330
As the feminine beauty
representing this mansion!

04:36.070 --> 04:37.850
Please sort the trash, Liszt-san.

04:37.850 --> 04:38.940
Why?!

04:39.790 --> 04:41.710
I'mma be the leader, then.

04:41.710 --> 04:42.670
Hey, no!

04:42.670 --> 04:44.210
Stop, Mozart, you nut!

04:44.210 --> 04:45.710
Senpai is the great leader!

04:45.710 --> 04:47.380
I'm the grand leader, then.

04:47.380 --> 04:49.290
Then Senpai is the true leader!

04:49.290 --> 04:50.660
No competing!

04:52.420 --> 04:53.730
All right, that's settled.

04:54.120 --> 04:55.350
Let's go with that.

04:55.350 --> 04:57.020
Hold it!

04:57.380 --> 05:01.350
What are these utterly useless tasks?

04:58.770 --> 05:01.900
Otowakan Chores List
Symbol - Liszt
Leader - Mozart
Background Music - Sousuke
Gaming Director - Chopin
Lead Guitar - Beethoven
Serious Guy - Schubert

05:02.110 --> 05:03.580
This is wrong!

05:03.580 --> 05:05.670
I want you to clean, do laundry,

05:05.670 --> 05:08.450
take care of Hasshie... Chores!

05:08.450 --> 05:10.240
Not all this pointless work!

05:11.410 --> 05:13.750
No, Chopin-san, this includes you.

05:14.510 --> 05:15.710
What now?

05:15.710 --> 05:16.910
Should we rock-paper-scissors it out?

05:16.910 --> 05:18.620
You aren't deciding, Mozart.

05:19.300 --> 05:22.470
Senpai, how should we move forward?

05:24.130 --> 05:25.020
Rock-paper-scissors.

05:27.150 --> 05:28.510
Understood.

05:28.800 --> 05:29.760
Listen up, everyone!

05:29.760 --> 05:30.600
Rock-paper-scissors!

05:30.990 --> 05:33.720
Could you hurry up and choose?

05:35.370 --> 05:37.560
Loser does the chores!

05:37.560 --> 05:39.580
Rock, paper, scissors!

05:39.940 --> 05:41.840
One more time!

05:42.240 --> 05:43.030
More!

05:43.360 --> 05:44.180
More!

05:44.440 --> 05:45.260
More!

05:45.560 --> 05:48.990
More! More! More!

05:46.670 --> 05:47.760
Ahem...

05:48.990 --> 05:49.950
More!

05:49.290 --> 05:49.950
Ahem!

05:49.950 --> 05:50.970
More?

05:50.970 --> 05:53.370
Why don't you do one-on-one?

05:53.370 --> 05:55.220
We're wasting time.

05:56.500 --> 05:58.500
Rock, paper, scissors.

06:01.000 --> 06:03.450
Wait, you threw your move late.

06:03.450 --> 06:04.270
What?

06:04.270 --> 06:05.300
Once more.

06:05.300 --> 06:06.860
No, I didn't.

06:06.860 --> 06:07.350
Did to!

06:07.350 --> 06:10.160
You were 0.0001 second earlier.

06:10.160 --> 06:12.250
That doesn't count as cheating.

06:10.540 --> 06:12.370
Senpai...

06:12.250 --> 06:13.510
Yes, it is.

06:12.840 --> 06:15.060
I definitely lose here.

06:15.420 --> 06:17.140
No, you won.

06:17.140 --> 06:18.280
I lose!

06:18.280 --> 06:19.560
You have to be the one to move forward...

06:19.800 --> 06:20.980
You win!

06:20.980 --> 06:22.810
Senpai!

06:23.110 --> 06:25.950
Cho-chan, I'm going to throw <i>paper</i>.

06:25.950 --> 06:26.510
Ready?

06:26.510 --> 06:28.350
Rock, paper, scissors!

06:30.040 --> 06:31.990
Welcome to the real world.

06:35.000 --> 06:37.630
Drawing straws is definitely the
most peaceful way to do it.

06:37.630 --> 06:38.670
Totally.

06:38.670 --> 06:40.800
I don't care, just hurry up!

06:47.550 --> 06:49.450
You looked inside.

06:50.770 --> 06:52.720
You...

06:52.720 --> 06:55.220
Why do you always cause Senpai trouble?

06:55.220 --> 06:56.680
I didn't look!
What, do you have proof, Lud-kun?

06:57.930 --> 06:58.860
Six!

06:58.860 --> 07:00.830
Yes!

07:00.830 --> 07:02.000
Not again.

07:02.000 --> 07:03.220
No, I didn't!

07:03.220 --> 07:05.580
I swear, I really didn't cheat this time.

07:05.860 --> 07:07.090
<i>This</i> time?

07:07.940 --> 07:10.030
So you <i>were</i> cheating!

07:10.030 --> 07:11.780
But how are you supposed to win if
you draw straws without cheating?

07:11.780 --> 07:16.990
What <i>will</i> work for you people?!

07:18.750 --> 07:20.290
Final Version

07:20.290 --> 07:21.750
Cleaning - Mozart (Super Leader)

07:21.750 --> 07:23.210
Laundry - Beethoven
(Ultimate Leader)
Sch S Sch Schubert

07:23.210 --> 07:24.670
Sch S Schu
Cooking - Liszt-san (Symbol)
Sousuke

07:24.670 --> 07:26.130
Taking Care of Hasshie - Chopin, Pad-kun

07:31.080 --> 07:33.380
What the hell is wrong with those freaks?

07:33.380 --> 07:34.730
Why do they exist?

07:34.730 --> 07:36.990
Why do they do nothing but cause me trouble?

07:39.130 --> 07:41.890
I definitely need a vacation.

07:41.890 --> 07:45.310
Izu

07:41.890 --> 07:45.310
Sightseeing
The Best Hot Spring Inns in Izu

07:42.200 --> 07:43.670
A villa in Izu...

07:43.670 --> 07:45.310
Uzuki's such an awesome friend.

07:45.730 --> 07:48.070
Travel time! I can't wait!

07:48.070 --> 07:49.280
Traveling where?

07:55.590 --> 07:56.580
What are you doing?

07:58.560 --> 08:01.340
What?! That was all a lie?!

08:01.690 --> 08:02.920
You're too loud!

08:02.920 --> 08:05.920
You said you were visiting your relatives!

08:05.030 --> 08:06.210
Uzuki said—

08:06.210 --> 08:08.580
Uzuki said she's visiting her relatives,

08:08.580 --> 08:10.670
so I'm coming with her.

08:10.670 --> 08:12.930
And we just <i>happen</i> to be staying at a villa.

08:12.930 --> 08:14.810
So I'm not lying, okay?

08:14.810 --> 08:15.450
Got it?

08:15.890 --> 08:17.420
Guys, it's a vacation!

08:17.420 --> 08:19.010
She's going on vacation!

08:21.450 --> 08:22.440
Sorry.

08:22.870 --> 08:26.660
But I can't take them all
on vacation with me.

08:26.660 --> 08:28.260
You said "vacation."

08:28.610 --> 08:30.350
I'll be home quick.

08:30.350 --> 08:33.750
I want you guys to take care of the
house for just a little while.

08:34.530 --> 08:35.490
But...

08:36.030 --> 08:39.240
with the way things are
going, I can't leave here.

08:39.610 --> 08:42.610
I thought I could finally get some
time to hang out with Uzuki and the others.

08:43.790 --> 08:45.690
Okay, okay.

08:45.690 --> 08:46.810
I get it.

08:48.430 --> 08:50.270
It's all right.

08:50.270 --> 08:52.460
You'll go to the villa. Okay?

08:55.440 --> 08:57.930
Why?!

08:58.600 --> 09:00.320
Why do you not work?!

09:00.320 --> 09:02.560
I followed the girl's instruction's!

09:02.560 --> 09:03.770
Power

09:02.560 --> 09:03.770
Program

09:02.960 --> 09:03.930
"Power on."

09:04.130 --> 09:05.360
"Put in laundry."

09:05.360 --> 09:07.140
"Parenthesis, 'But always check

09:07.140 --> 09:09.590
pockets first,' closing parenthesis"

09:09.940 --> 09:14.100
"Select Normal mode, pour
detergent and softener,

09:14.100 --> 09:16.180
and finally, hit Start."

09:20.520 --> 09:21.740
Spielen...

09:22.420 --> 09:24.660
wir unsere...

09:23.870 --> 09:25.000
Hang on a second!

09:25.340 --> 09:28.280
Why are you trying to use
your Musik, Beethes-san?

09:28.280 --> 09:30.320
What if the washing machine
gets up and starts dancing?

09:30.320 --> 09:31.090
Please, no!

09:31.090 --> 09:32.470
It's no use.

09:32.470 --> 09:33.940
It can't be done.

09:34.510 --> 09:35.970
It's all right.

09:35.970 --> 09:36.880
Spielen...

09:36.880 --> 09:38.510
Don't!

09:41.800 --> 09:43.090
Let's go.

09:43.090 --> 09:43.970
Yeah.

09:48.300 --> 09:49.320
It was the lid.

09:53.070 --> 09:55.030
It's all right, Chopin-san.

09:55.030 --> 09:56.860
There's nothing to be afraid of.

09:58.490 --> 10:00.000
It's just a bird.

10:00.000 --> 10:01.660
And I'm a machine.

10:01.660 --> 10:05.570
There isn't a single human in sight to fear.

10:06.950 --> 10:09.700
That's it, good, Chopin-san.

10:09.700 --> 10:12.510
Good. You can do it.

10:14.250 --> 10:16.860
But let's take it a little faster, shall we?

10:16.860 --> 10:20.670
At this rate, it'll take you until
August, six years from now.

10:21.720 --> 10:23.770
Oh, Chopin-san!

10:25.300 --> 10:27.330
See? Everyone's doing their best.

10:27.680 --> 10:28.430
Yeah.

10:29.050 --> 10:30.370
Let's go.

10:30.670 --> 10:31.340
Yeah.

10:35.040 --> 10:37.700
Yay! Yahoo!

10:38.350 --> 10:39.880
Damn barbarian.

10:39.880 --> 10:43.040
Why must I clean with this man?

10:43.040 --> 10:45.330
I wanted to use the laundry
machine with Senpai.

10:50.250 --> 10:52.770
Keep doing your shoddy work.

10:52.770 --> 10:54.860
I'm going to work slow and steady,

10:54.860 --> 10:56.870
and do perfect work.

10:56.870 --> 10:59.770
You'll be the one who gets scolded by the

10:59.770 --> 11:01.830
landlady in the very end, Mozart.

11:03.200 --> 11:05.310
This is difficult, though.

11:05.570 --> 11:08.090
What is the best position for this?

11:11.130 --> 11:13.580
Kanae, I'm done.

11:13.580 --> 11:14.980
Already?

11:15.800 --> 11:17.830
He probably hasn't cleaned it well.

11:17.830 --> 11:19.160
Now, receive your scolding.

11:19.160 --> 11:21.190
Receive it, Mozart!

11:22.450 --> 11:24.640
It's a bit rough,

11:24.640 --> 11:26.670
but well, this house is big.

11:26.670 --> 11:29.510
I'd appreciate if you
could keep up the pace.

11:29.510 --> 11:30.840
Thanks, Motes.

11:31.810 --> 11:33.600
Okay, could you do the dining room next?

11:33.600 --> 11:34.570
Okay.

11:35.270 --> 11:37.050
I-Impossible.

11:37.330 --> 11:38.450
Impossible!

11:39.730 --> 11:40.910
Schu-san...

11:42.230 --> 11:44.290
You don't need to be so nitpicky.

11:44.290 --> 11:46.400
Could you be a bit quicker?

11:46.750 --> 11:48.560
Learn from Motes.

11:52.710 --> 11:53.690
Schu-san?

11:56.130 --> 11:59.450
What is the best position
for the symbol to be,

11:59.750 --> 12:01.240
here in this mansion?

12:02.640 --> 12:03.380
No.

12:04.900 --> 12:06.160
No.

12:08.490 --> 12:10.180
Definitely not.

12:11.990 --> 12:13.330
Where do I go?

12:14.360 --> 12:15.800
This is good exercise.

12:19.960 --> 12:21.860
That's it, Chopin-san!

12:21.860 --> 12:22.840
Amazing!

12:23.070 --> 12:25.760
You're definitely growing as a person.

12:27.930 --> 12:29.810
Hurry up, Schu-kun.

12:31.360 --> 12:32.650
Mozart!

12:32.650 --> 12:35.560
Are you not scared, Mozart?

12:35.900 --> 12:37.500
Why are you here?

12:37.500 --> 12:39.790
Weren't you asked to do
the dining hall next?

12:39.790 --> 12:43.400
I bet Kanae will be really happy
if the roof is suddenly clean.

12:46.690 --> 12:48.410
Are you scared?

12:48.410 --> 12:49.870
You don't have to force yourself.

12:49.870 --> 12:51.580
I-I'm not scared.

12:51.580 --> 12:53.730
Who do you think I am?

12:54.120 --> 12:56.880
You really don't have to push yourself.

12:56.880 --> 12:59.040
I just invited you because
I thought you might want

12:59.040 --> 13:00.800
Kanae to say good things about you.

13:00.800 --> 13:02.950
I heard her calling you "slow" earlier.

13:02.350 --> 13:04.040
She never—

13:04.040 --> 13:06.140
She never called me "slow"!

13:06.460 --> 13:07.140
Here.

13:08.690 --> 13:10.620
Come on. It's dangerous.

13:16.230 --> 13:17.830
Hey, a blimp.

13:19.320 --> 13:21.490
Mozart!

13:21.490 --> 13:22.910
Schu-kun!

13:24.600 --> 13:26.270
Are you all right?

13:28.300 --> 13:29.450
Senpai...

13:31.790 --> 13:32.950
Spielen...

13:33.330 --> 13:34.550
Wait, please!

13:34.550 --> 13:35.890
...wir unsere...

13:35.890 --> 13:36.780
It's not what it looks like!

13:36.780 --> 13:38.640
This is all Mozart's...

13:51.470 --> 13:52.960
Oh, you.

13:53.790 --> 13:55.630
Imitating Wolf again?

14:02.360 --> 14:03.520
Schu-kun?

14:06.150 --> 14:08.680
We're here, Chopin-san!

14:08.680 --> 14:09.570
Almost there.

14:09.860 --> 14:11.050
Hang in there.

14:11.050 --> 14:12.450
Take it slow.

14:12.830 --> 14:14.540
Magnificent.

14:14.990 --> 14:16.460
You've finally done it!

14:16.940 --> 14:18.280
Delivery.

14:20.030 --> 14:21.770
You're freaking kidding me!

14:21.770 --> 14:22.600
You asshole!

14:22.600 --> 14:24.340
We were in the middle of something, idiot!

14:24.340 --> 14:25.590
Leave!

14:36.730 --> 14:38.150
I can't...

14:38.150 --> 14:40.760
I can't find a place to be the symbol.

14:41.150 --> 14:42.990
I'm a failure.

14:44.020 --> 14:45.820
What is this? What's gotten into you?

14:49.030 --> 14:50.880
Ow...

14:51.320 --> 14:52.500
Motes-san.

14:52.500 --> 14:54.120
What are you doing? Are you okay?

14:54.120 --> 14:56.490
This is terrible.

14:56.490 --> 14:57.910
It snapped on me.

15:03.880 --> 15:05.530
What the hell?
What happened?

15:05.530 --> 15:07.090
What did you do, Motes-san?

15:07.380 --> 15:11.300
I couldn't get the dirt off, so
I thought it might be cute if I made it pink.

15:11.710 --> 15:12.980
And then...

15:15.350 --> 15:17.380
Don't "teehee" me.

15:18.640 --> 15:19.720
You screwed up!

15:19.720 --> 15:21.300
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

15:22.610 --> 15:24.020
Who are you?

15:24.420 --> 15:26.380
What are we going to do about this?

15:26.380 --> 15:29.100
She's going to do more than just
cry when she sees this.

15:29.100 --> 15:30.090
We're erasing it.

15:30.960 --> 15:32.270
What else?

15:32.270 --> 15:33.770
Before the little kitten finds out.

15:33.770 --> 15:34.720
Hurry!

15:35.310 --> 15:36.800
We're erasing it?!

15:36.800 --> 15:38.750
Quit whining and—

15:39.700 --> 15:42.090
You idiots, we don't need that!

15:42.090 --> 15:42.750
But...

15:43.000 --> 15:45.010
Just listen. I have an Idea.

15:48.580 --> 15:49.710
Symbol!

15:54.010 --> 15:55.360
This is perfect.

15:55.360 --> 15:56.700
I belonged here all along.

15:56.700 --> 15:59.430
You're not going to fool her.
Help us clean!

15:59.860 --> 16:01.400
Hurry!

16:01.770 --> 16:03.760
Why are we erasing it?

16:03.760 --> 16:05.660
Pink is so cute.

16:05.660 --> 16:07.210
Shut up and wipe.

16:07.510 --> 16:09.080
Okay, but who are you?

16:09.750 --> 16:10.830
No good.

16:10.830 --> 16:12.230
It's not working.

16:12.230 --> 16:14.410
I'm going to get more rags.

16:18.300 --> 16:19.910
My work is finally complete.

16:20.340 --> 16:22.420
I've opened the path to my fate.

16:22.420 --> 16:24.550
Now, feel the wind,

16:24.550 --> 16:27.000
my laundry!

16:31.210 --> 16:33.130
H-How dare you!

16:33.130 --> 16:35.240
Sorry, Beethes-san, it's an emergency.

16:35.240 --> 16:36.890
Sorry, Lud-kun.

16:37.540 --> 16:40.660
We've ruined all of Senpai's hard work.

16:41.540 --> 16:43.270
Wh-Who is that?

16:43.480 --> 16:46.400
Could you keep an eye out
for my little kitten?

16:46.400 --> 16:47.230
Why?

16:47.230 --> 16:49.270
Can't you tell from the situation?

16:49.270 --> 16:52.180
She'll kick us out, if she sees this.

16:52.580 --> 16:53.810
Don't let her out.

16:53.810 --> 16:55.140
Don't let her see the roof.

16:57.370 --> 16:58.400
Ack!

16:58.400 --> 16:59.590
Keep it together.

17:00.800 --> 17:02.650
Again, you aren't fooling her!

17:02.650 --> 17:04.000
Quit messing around!

17:04.900 --> 17:06.670
Beethes, what are you doing here?

17:11.730 --> 17:13.220
Hey, are you listening?

17:17.140 --> 17:19.400
I'm going shopping for dinner.

17:19.400 --> 17:21.410
Tell everyone not to slack.

17:27.500 --> 17:29.320
Jeez, what's your problem?

17:29.980 --> 17:32.440
I-I need to talk to you.

17:32.870 --> 17:34.970
Talk? About what?

17:36.120 --> 17:38.210
I can't say it here.

17:39.650 --> 17:40.780
When I get back, then.

17:40.780 --> 17:42.720
It's an important talk!

17:44.650 --> 17:46.140
P-Please.

17:46.790 --> 17:49.580
Let's go back inside.

17:49.980 --> 17:50.870
I want to talk.

17:51.900 --> 17:53.560
An important talk.

17:54.010 --> 17:55.020
Okay.

17:58.720 --> 18:00.800
Oh, what about laundry?

18:01.100 --> 18:02.340
Are you done?

18:02.670 --> 18:05.010
The l-laundry

18:05.310 --> 18:07.640
is d-done.

18:07.640 --> 18:10.440
Are you sure?
Did you hang it out to dry?

18:13.530 --> 18:15.930
Wh-What? Beethes...

18:16.900 --> 18:17.680
Hey!

18:20.290 --> 18:22.900
Is he going to give me the<i> talk?</i>

18:23.880 --> 18:25.410
Are you serious?

18:29.150 --> 18:30.700
I-I mean,

18:31.000 --> 18:34.510
I'm flattered, but...

18:35.500 --> 18:37.720
I'm still a student.

18:37.980 --> 18:39.900
There are some things

18:39.900 --> 18:42.470
I like about you,

18:42.870 --> 18:43.680
but...

18:44.080 --> 18:47.310
She's making a huge mistake!

18:47.310 --> 18:49.030
I-I'm sorry.

18:50.860 --> 18:51.990
I can't.

18:55.470 --> 18:57.480
R-Rejected!

18:57.480 --> 18:59.060
And he wasn't even asking her out!

18:59.060 --> 19:02.130
Beethes-san kind of got
rejected one-sidedly.

19:02.130 --> 19:02.730
Jesus!

19:02.730 --> 19:04.490
I'm sorry, Senpai, but that's hilarious.

19:08.710 --> 19:11.000
Beethes? I...

19:13.350 --> 19:14.060
Th-

19:14.590 --> 19:17.480
That's understandable.

19:18.050 --> 19:19.420
He's playing along!

19:19.420 --> 19:20.840
Good job, Lud-kun!

19:20.840 --> 19:21.570
Good for you!

19:21.570 --> 19:23.020
Senpai!

19:31.290 --> 19:33.020
Hey, what is this?

19:34.820 --> 19:35.780
Beethes!

19:36.620 --> 19:38.030
What's wrong, Beethes?

19:38.560 --> 19:41.000
Y-You saw.

19:42.020 --> 19:44.680
Yes. We ClassicaLoids vomit this

19:44.680 --> 19:47.030
pink-colored soup when

19:47.290 --> 19:49.710
we're hurt emotionally.

19:50.640 --> 19:51.560
Soup?

19:52.240 --> 19:53.490
Soup?

19:56.490 --> 19:58.200
It's because I rejected you, isn't it?

19:58.200 --> 19:59.870
Is that why this is happening?

20:00.270 --> 20:01.760
I'm sorry, Beethes.

20:01.760 --> 20:03.680
I'm sure you'll find someone nice.

20:03.910 --> 20:06.430
Let's just go inside, okay?

20:07.770 --> 20:10.610
H-He actually managed to keep her fooled.

20:10.610 --> 20:12.230
Not bad, Lud-kun.

20:12.230 --> 20:13.730
Don't waste time.

20:13.730 --> 20:14.520
Now's our chance.

20:26.640 --> 20:30.450
It's the emotional damage of not being
able to be the symbol of the mansion.

20:31.130 --> 20:33.870
I can't believe Lud-kun would be rejected.

20:33.870 --> 20:35.540
My heart!

20:36.080 --> 20:37.090
Likewise.

20:37.090 --> 20:39.000
I'm so sorry, Senpai.

20:39.750 --> 20:41.300
Poor Beethes.

20:48.000 --> 20:49.430
Sousuke, you too?!

20:51.360 --> 20:52.310
Hasshie, you too?

20:52.310 --> 20:54.630
Th-There's a theory that
not just ClassicaLoids,

20:54.630 --> 20:57.640
but also humans and shoebills,

20:57.640 --> 21:00.820
expel pink soup when hurt emotionally.

21:01.070 --> 21:04.050
Oh, really?

21:05.740 --> 21:07.130
I'm going shopping.

21:08.350 --> 21:11.400
Have it all cleaned up
by the time I get back.

21:11.850 --> 21:12.550
Or else...

21:18.320 --> 21:19.790
Hurry, hurry!

21:19.790 --> 21:21.270
We probably don't have even half an hour!

21:21.270 --> 21:22.380
We need to start with the roof.

21:22.380 --> 21:23.580
Go, go!

21:23.580 --> 21:26.540
W-Wait, let me take a break.

21:26.540 --> 21:27.920
Senpai, hurry!

21:27.920 --> 21:28.950
I was just rejected!

21:28.950 --> 21:30.800
Let me rest a little!

22:05.010 --> 22:06.630
All right, that's it.

22:06.950 --> 22:09.420
I've made up my mind!

22:13.890 --> 22:15.410
Kanae's late.

22:15.410 --> 22:17.120
Maybe she can't make it today.

22:17.120 --> 22:19.650
She said something about having
to do something at home.

22:19.950 --> 22:21.540
Uzuki!

22:21.540 --> 22:22.260
Kana—

22:28.860 --> 22:30.910
Sorry we're late.

22:30.910 --> 22:31.820
Let's go.

22:31.820 --> 22:34.190
Wait, Kanae, this won't work.

22:34.190 --> 22:35.960
Let's go, kids!

22:35.960 --> 22:37.610
Yes, ma'am.

22:38.970 --> 22:40.980
Seriously, this isn't good.

22:41.280 --> 22:42.140
Kanae!

22:42.960 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

22:43.000 --> 22:45.220
Kanae!

24:15.970 --> 24:17.970
12: "J. S. Bach"

24:16.580 --> 24:18.970
Beethes speaks, Motes nods:
Art is a howl and

24:17.640 --> 24:19.220
Arkhe Corporation Hosts
28th New Artist Audition

24:18.970 --> 24:22.510
glimmer of the free mind,
from deep within.

24:22.510 --> 24:25.090
Alas, Great Bach says:
"Freedom, by any name,

24:22.850 --> 24:24.400
Musik Activation Report

24:24.400 --> 24:25.810
Musik Activation Report

24:25.090 --> 24:27.220
is fleeting, and leads only to stagnation."

24:27.220 --> 24:29.140
Wh-Which is true?
